1. Before any parsing happens, `opt` loads `build/libMiniShield.so` through `-load-pass-plugin` (`dlopen`) and calls the exported `llvmGetPassPluginInfo()`. The returned `PassPluginLibraryInfo` includes the callback that calls `PB.registerPipelineParsingCallback(...)`, which installs the function-pipeline parsing callback with the `PassBuilder`.
2. When the pipeline parser reaches the element inside `function(minishield-flatten)`, it hands the name `minishield-flatten` to the registered callback, together with the `FunctionPassManager` (`FPM`) and the inner pipeline (empty for a simple name).
