4. Parser: “unknown function pass 'minishield-stats'” means the loaded plugin's parsing callback did not recognize the name — it is not registered, or the pipeline string is misspelled.
5. The stale-`.so` warning: a failed build leaves the previous `libMiniShield.so` on disk, and it loads successfully. An unknown-pass error seen through that old file does not test your newly edited callback at all, because the new callback was never compiled into it. Rebuild successfully first, then rerun `opt` — only then does the error, or its absence, say anything about the new registration.

